@parklandspamoja

Ahead of #Innovate4Cities in Nairobi, it was a pleasure to host a breakfast bringing together partners from private, public and development sectors to discuss how finance and partnerships can turn climate commitments to implementation at scale. 

There was strong convergence on the need to move from ambition to action.

It was also an opportunity to share perspectives on Sweden's international approach to collaboration with cities through the forthcoming Team Sweden Smart Cities Strategy 2026–2030: Sweden – A Partner for Cities Globally.

Thank you to all who participated at the start of this busy week and a special thanks to the Deputy Governor of Nairobi @JNjorogeMuchiri for his attendance and participation. Thanks
